Z||000000||jhar||10-04-1999||07:29 PM||||i have been trying to get my 2.5 to idle correctly since aug. still having no luck. cold starts are the problem, sometimes the idle rpm is prefect other times it starts out at 500rpm and you fight it till its warm. then this morning it cold idled at 800rpm when i first started it and would barely stay running. then i turned on the heater and the idle went to 1800rpm? shut the heater off back down to 500rpm! i have replaced everything but ecm, could i have a bad sensor that is supposed to be new or what???thanks||||reg||8
Z||000001||Lynx||10-05-1999||01:31 PM||||I have a 85 2.5 that hates the cold too but only hesitates at take off not idle bad. It only idles bad cold when i have the A&C on. Also did you change the temp sensor to the ECM if it is bad the car will think it is warm and wont run right. Also i would check your electrical system and make sure there is no short or ground loops. I have say some home made Fiero wiring systems before not a pretty sight.||||reg||12
Z||000002||theogre||10-05-1999||03:36 PM||||activating heater turns on the AC in some positions which will run up the idle.<P>Exactly what have you replaced?<P>Hook it up to an ECM scanner and watch it in real time.... if it's a sensor you should be able to narrow it down really fast.||||reg||1
